# Build artifacts
build/
src/build/
build-cov/
build-static/
*.o
*.d

# Per-binary gcov payloads, written into the repository root by the coverage
# script and cleaned by `make coverage-clean`.
*.gcov.json.gz

# Generated by the build into the repository root (templates in scripts/)
/ktplace.sh
/ktplace.csh

# Generated placements, plots, logs and suite drivers: a run writes here, so
# nothing in it belongs in the commit.
output/
out.pl

# Run transcript
ktplace.log
*.log

# Benchmark data is downloaded, not committed: keep the directory itself
# visible so the fetch script and its docs can be tracked.
benchmark/*
!benchmark/fetch_benchmarks.py
!benchmark/README.md

# Two designs are the exceptions, and both are deliberate: one per feature that
# CI has to be able to test without depending on a download.
#
# adaptec1 is the smoke design. The whole design is 5.4 MB already gzipped, which
# is a fair price for a smoke test that cannot break on someone else's uptime;
# fetch_benchmarks.py downloads the other seven from the contest site. The
# contest evaluators of 2005 and 2006 are committed too, with their wrappers.
!benchmark/ISPD_2005/
benchmark/ISPD_2005/*
!benchmark/ISPD_2005/adaptec1/
!benchmark/ISPD_2005/evaluator/
!benchmark/ISPD06/
benchmark/ISPD06/*
!benchmark/ISPD06/evaluator/

# ibm01 is the multi-row legalization design: 120 of its movable cells are taller
# than a row, so it is the only benchmark here that exercises that path at all,
# and the only one whose legality CI can assert deterministically (12,380 cells,
# under a second to legalize). Its suite *is* fetchable, but a fetch of 23 designs
# to get one is a bad trade for a CI job that has to run on every push. Gzipped
# it is 436 KB, a sixth of adaptec1.
!benchmark/ICCAD04/
benchmark/ICCAD04/*
!benchmark/ICCAD04/ibm01/

# Editor / OS noise
*.swp
.DS_Store
.claude
.opencode
logs/

# Local editor tooling (kept out of the repo)
.cursorrules
# Development notes are ignored; the curated write-ups are tracked.
docs/*
!docs/simpl.md
!docs/docker.md
!docs/visualization.md
!docs/images/
ref/
*.whl

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# clangd compilation database: regenerated by `make compile-commands`.
# The include paths are absolute, so a committed copy is wrong elsewhere, and a
# stale one makes clangd report diagnostics from flags the build does not use.
compile_commands.json

# Default work-directory output: a run with no -w writes into the current
# directory, so these land in the repo root.
placed.pl
plots/
